{"graph_chars": "Demand and supply is the second fundamental diagram in this course. The opportunity set from Chapter Two was the first. Do not memorize every example. Learn the model. Horizontal axis: quantity of a good, of labor, or of financial capital. Vertical axis: price, wage, or rate of return. One event can only shift demand right, demand left, supply right, or supply left. Isolate each change. You do not need to know why a Hawaii ticket is expensive this week. The price already bundled demand, jet fuel, and the airline's experiment. Fly or wait. An oat farmer does not need the health study. The higher oat price says: grow more. Price controls try to kill the messenger. Killing the messenger never killed the news, and other messengers stop coming. China's Great Leap Forward in the late nineteen fifties kept food prices artificially low. Farm production collapsed. Thirty to forty million people died of starvation. Immobilizing the price messenger hides scarcity. Buyers and sellers then cannot react.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0648], [0.0648, 0.1295], [0.1295, 0.1943], [0.1943, 0.2591], [0.2591, 0.3238], [0.3238, 0.3886], [0.3886, 0.4534], [0.4534, 0.5181], [0.5181, 0.5829], [0.5829, 0.6477], [0.6477, 0.7124], [0.7124, 0.7772], [0.7772, 0.842], [0.842, 0.9067], [0.9067, 0.9715], [0.9715, 1.0363], [1.0363, 1.101], [1.101, 1.1658], [1.1658, 1.2306], [1.2306, 1.2953], [1.2953, 1.3601], [1.3601, 1.4249], [1.4249, 1.4896], [1.4896, 1.5544], [1.5544, 1.6192], [1.6192, 1.6839], [1.6839, 1.7487], [1.7487, 1.8135], [1.8135, 1.8782], [1.8782, 1.943], [1.943, 2.0078], [2.0078, 2.0725], [2.0725, 2.1373], [2.1373, 2.202], [2.202, 2.2668], [2.2668, 2.3316], [2.3316, 2.3963], [2.3963, 2.4611], [2.4611, 2.5259], [2.5259, 2.5906], [2.5906, 2.6554], [2.6554, 2.7202], [2.7202, 2.7849], [2.7849, 2.8497], [2.8497, 2.9145], [2.9145, 2.9792], [2.9792, 3.044], [3.044, 3.1088], [3.1088, 3.1735], [3.1735, 3.2383], [3.2383, 3.3031], [3.3031, 3.3678], [3.3678, 3.4326], [3.4326, 3.4974], 